Clearing the caches
Old caches take room and keep nothing
you need.

Command
  app clean

What it is
  A cache is a copy kept so a second
  read is quick; it can always be made
  again.

Found on this machine
  - 3 caches, 2.1 GB
  - the oldest is from March

Why it matters
  A full disk stops builds, and the
  caches are the part that is safe to
  give back.

What the change does
  Removes the cache folders it lists,
  and nothing else.

What it does not do
  Touch a project, a setting or anything
  outside the cache folders.

How to undo it
  There is nothing to undo; the next
  build makes the caches again, slower
  once.

How to check it
  Run app clean again: it finds nothing
  to remove.

In this program's documents
  - docs/caches.md

Outside sources
  - https://example.test/caches
